|''[[Skyrim:Horses|Horses]] and horse-drawn carriages are common means of transportation in Skyrim. Both can handle the harsh terrain with ease.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenHorseMulti.nif||[[File:SR-load-Horses and horse-drawn carriages.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''In some of Skyrim's darkest recesses, where the living fear to tread, the bones of the dead still walk. These [[Skyrim:Skeleton|Skeletons]] feel no pain or remorse... and deserve no mercy.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenSkeleton.nif||[[File:SR-load-In some of Skyrim's darkest recesses.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Little is known of the mysterious [[Skyrim:Spriggan|Spriggans]], save that they revere Skyrim's forested regions, and will defend these regions with their lives.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenSpriggan.nif||[[File:SR-load-Little is known of the mysterious Spriggans.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Lurker|Lurkers]] are thought to be native to the murky waters of Hermaeus Mora's realm of [[Skyrim:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]].''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenLurker01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Lurkers are thought to be native.jpg|96px]]||3% chance of appearing if [[Skyrim:The Fate of the Skaal|The Fate of the Skaal]] is completed and the player is in Solstheim or [[Skyrim:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]].
|-
|''[[Skyrim:Mammoth|Mammoths]] are a common sight in the tundra of Skyrim, and are often herded by the Giants that also call that region home. They are generally peaceful creatures, unless provoked.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMammoth.nif||[[File:SR-load-Mammoths.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Many of Skyrim's waterways are home to [[Skyrim:Slaughterfish|Slaughterfish]], whose razor-sharp teeth have claimed the lives of many careless swimmers.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSlaughterFish.nif||[[File:SR-load-Many of Skyrim's waterways are home to Slaughterfish.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Many species of [[Skyrim:Bear|bear]] roam Skyrim's wilds. They are fearsome creatures, but will often avoid attacking unless provoked.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBearBrown.nif||[[File:SR-load-Many species of bear roam Skyrim's wilds.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Most of the [[Skyrim:Dog|dogs]] in Skyrim are domesticated, and serve as faithful companions to their Nord masters.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDog.nif||[[File:SR-load-Most of the dogs in Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Netch|Netch]] are often domesticated on the Morrowind mainland. Wild netch were first sighted on Solstheim several decades ago, perhaps drawn by the familiar flora that has grown up in the southern ashlands.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenNetch01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Netch are often domesticated.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|''No one is quite sure why the [[Skyrim:Draugr|Draugr]] walk the halls of Skyrim's burial crypts, but some believe they once served the dragons ages ago... and have been cursed with undeath for their treachery.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenMaleDraugr.nif||[[File:SR-load-No one is quite sure why the Draugr.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Of all the [[Lore:Dwemer_Animunculi|automatons]] left behind by the ancient [[Lore:Dwemer|Dwemer]], the [[Skyrim:Dwarven Centurion|Dwarven Centurions]] are among the most technologically impressive... and deadly. They guard [[Skyrim:Dwarven_Ruins|Dwemer ruins]] as if their masters still walked the halls.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSteam.nif||[[File:SR-load-Of all the automatons left behind.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''One of the most dangerous Steam Animunculi is the [[Skyrim:Dwarven Ballista|Dwarven Ballista]], which fires a bolt that can penetrate even the thickest armor.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBallista01.nif||[[File:SR-load-One of the most dangerous Steam Animunculi is the Dwarven Ballista.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Riekling|Rieklings]] have little culture of their own, but scavenge what relics they can from around Solstheim and form strange attachments to what they find.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenRiekling02.nif||[[File:SR-load-Rieklings have little culture of their own.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''Rieklings may be small in stature, but they attack in swarms and can be fearsome in melee combat. They are even known to tame and ride [[Skyrim:Bristleback|boars]] into battle.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenRiekling01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Rieklings may be small in stature.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Seeker|Seekers]] are servants of Hermaeus Mora. They are rarely seen outside his [[Lore:Oblivion|Oblivion]] realm of [[Skyrim:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]].''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSeeker01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Seekers are servants of Hermaeus Mora.jpg|96px]]||3% chance of appearing if [[Skyrim:The Temple of Miraak|The Temple of Miraak]] is completed and the player is in Solstheim or Apocrypha.
|-
|''[[Skyrim:Skeever|Skeevers]] are large, rat-like creatures that make their nests in caves, sewers, and underground warrens. While easy to kill, they can be a challenge in groups, and carry debilitating diseases.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSkeever.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skeevers.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Skyrim's [[Skyrim:Horker|Horkers]] are often hunted for their tusks and meat.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenHorker1.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skyrim's Horkers.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The ancient and long-dead Dwemer built many devices and automatons that continue to function even today, thanks to their advanced magic and technology. The [[Skyrim:Dwarven Spider|Dwarven Spider]] is one such construct.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDwarvenSpider.nif||[[File:SR-load-The ancient and long-dead Dwemer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The common [[Skyrim:Mudcrab|Mudcrab]] can be found by the [[Skyrim:Sea_of_Ghosts|northern shoreline]] or along the banks of any [[Skyrim:Bodies_of_Water|lakes or rivers]]. When not moving, it is easy to mistake for a rock, and uses this natural camouflage to ambush unwary prey.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMudcrab.nif||[[File:SR-load-The common Mudcrab.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Cow|cow]] is one of Skyrim's most common domestic animals. It provides the native Nords with meat, milk, and furs.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenCow.nif||[[File:SR-load-The cow.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Falmer|Falmer]] are twisted, evil creatures that dwell in Skyrim's deepest reaches. They have but one desire - to destroy the surface world, and any who dwell above.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenFalmer02.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Falmer are twisted.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Frostbite_Spider|Frostbite Spider]] is one of Skyrim's most fearsome and loathed native creatures. It will attack anyone relentlessly with both poison and fangs, and is as deadly as the affliction for which it was named.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenFrostbiteSpider.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Frostbite Spider.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The horses of Skyrim are hardy and strong, and make up for in endurance what they lack in speed.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenHorseMulti.nif||[[File:SR-load-The horses of Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Sabre_Cat|Sabre Cat]] of Skyrim is a giant, ferocious predator, and will often ambush travelers who stray too far from the roads, and into the wilds.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSabreCat.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Sabre Cat of Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The wilds of Skyrim are teeming with [[Skyrim:Deer|deer]]. They are docile creatures, but serve as food for much of the province's more savage beasts.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDeer.nif||[[File:SR-load-The wilds of Skyrim are teeming with deer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Wolf|wolves]] of Skyrim are feral, savage beasts, and hunt in packs to take down any prey available... be it animal or man.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenWolves.nif||[[File:SR-load-The wolves of Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Those venturing in Skyrim's deepest underground reaches should be wary of the [[Skyrim:Chaurus|Chaurus]], a giant insect that spits poison and bites with its razor-sharp mandibles.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenChurus.nif||[[File:SR-load-Those venturing in Skyrim's deepest underground reaches.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''What the [[Skyrim:Dwarven_Sphere|Dwarven Sphere]] lacks in strength it makes up for in speed and mobility, as it patrols the halls of the Dwemer ruins it still protects.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSphere.nif||[[File:SR-load-What the Dwarven Sphere lacks.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DG|alt}}''When a Chaurus reaches the end of its life, its body undergoes a dramatic transformation. After days of death-like stillness, the [[Skyrim:Chaurus_Hunter|Chaurus Hunter]] bursts free from the husk of the Chaurus.''||DLC01\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenCharHunter01.nif||[[File:SR-load-When a Chaurus reaches the end of its life.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''While Hagravens can be deadly with their claws in close combat, they can prove equally challenging at a distance, when casting Destruction spells.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenHagraven01.nif||[[File:SR-load-While Hagravens can be deadly.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Woe to the unwary explorer who delves deep into the burial crypts of the ancient Nords, and disturbs the Draugr that dwell within.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDraugrFemale.nif||[[File:SR-load-Woe to the unwary explorer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Years of living underground have rendered the Falmer blind, but their other senses have become more acute as a result.''||rowspan=2| LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenFalmer01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Years of living underground.jpg|96px]]||rowspan=2|
|-
|{{DG|alt}}''Scholars assume that generations of living underground rendered the Falmer blind. Over time their other senses have become more acute as a result.''||[[File:SR-load-Scholars assume that generations.jpg|96px]]
|-
!colspan=4|
=====[[Skyrim:Dragon|Dragons]]=====
|-
|''And [[Skyrim:Elder_Scroll|the Scrolls]] have foretold, of black wings in the cold, That when brothers wage war come unfurled! [[Skyrim:Alduin|Alduin]], Bane of Kings, ancient shadow unbound, With a hunger to swallow the world! -- [[Skyrim:Songs_of_Skyrim|Song of the Dragonborn]]||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenAlduinWall.nif||[[File:SR-load-And the Scrolls have foretold.jpg|96px]]||Started new game.
|-
|''In days of old, when dragons ruled the earth, there lived mortal men who [[Lore:Dragon_Cult|worshipped]] the beasts as gods. These [[Skyrim:Dragon_Priest|Dragon Priests]] are long since dead... but something has awoken them from their ancient slumber.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDragonPriest.nif||[[File:SR-load-In days of old, when dragons ruled the earth.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|rowspan=2|''Most Nords of Skyrim assumed the dragons were only a legend. Until now.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBronzeDragon.nif||[[File:SR-load-Most Nords of Skyrim assumed (bronze).jpg|96px]]||
|-
|LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenOdahviing.nif||[[File:SR-load-Most Nords of Skyrim assumed (Odahviing).jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Once, the dragons sought to eliminate or enslave all mortal races. If given the chance, they would surely do so again...''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenFrostDragon1.nif||[[File:SR-load-Once, the dragons sought to eliminate.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DG|alt}}''Revered and legendary dragons are more deadly than ancient dragons. They use a shout that can drain health, magicka and stamina from its victims.''||DLC01\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenLegDragon01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Revered and legendary dragons.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''When a dragon uses a breath attack like fire or frost, it is speaking in an ancient and powerful language. A battle between two dragons is actually a deadly verbal debate.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenFrostDragon1.nif||[[File:SR-load-When a dragon uses a breath attack.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''While all dragons are fearsome, some are more powerful than others. Brown and green-skinned dragons are generally weaker than their white or bronze-skinned cousins.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenSwampDragon1.nif||[[File:SR-load-While all dragons are fearsome.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
=====[[Skyrim:Troll|Trolls]]=====
|-
|{{DG|alt}}''The Dawnguard has [[Skyrim:Armored_Troll|armored battle trolls]] that they use when fighting vampires.''||DLC01\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenArmoredTroll01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Dawnguard has armored battle trolls.jpg|96px]]||Completed [[Skyrim:Bloodline|Bloodline]], 3% chance.
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Frost_Troll|Frost Troll]] is the most fearsome of its kind found in Skyrim, and is at home in the province's most frozen regions.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenTroll.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Frost Troll.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Trolls can be found in any region throughout Skyrim, both deep underground or wandering the wilds.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenTrollCave.nif||[[File:SR-load-Trolls can be found in any region.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Trolls regenerate health when wounded, but are susceptible to fire.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadscreenTrollClean.nif||[[File:SR-load-Trolls regenerate health.jpg|96px]]||
|}
