====[[Skyrim:College_of_Winterhold_(faction)|College of Winterhold]]====
|-
|''Most of Winterhold was lost to the sea in the [[Lore:Great_Collapse|Great Collapse]] of {{Year|4E 122}}, but the College was left mysteriously unharmed.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenWinterholdShield.nif||[[File:SR-load-Most of Winterhold was lost.jpg|96px]]||rowspan=4| In [[Skyrim:Winterhold|Winterhold]] or [[Skyrim:College of Winterhold (place)|College of Winterhold]], 16% chance.
|-
|''Once a source of pride for the people of Winterhold, the College is now shunned and feared.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBretonMage.nif||[[File:SR-load-Once a source of pride for the people of Winterhold.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''The College of Winterhold is an independent organization, and thus was not affected by the dissolution of the [[Lore:Mages_Guild|Mages Guild]] at the beginning of the [[Lore:Fourth_Era|Fourth Era]].''||Architecture\Winterhold\{{zwsp}}WinterholdSymbol01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The College of Winterhold is an independent organization.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''While the mages of the College of Winterhold gladly share knowledge amongst themselves, they do not offer most services to the rest of Skyrim.''||Architecture\Winterhold\{{zwsp}}MageStatue.nif||[[File:SR-load-While the mages of the College of Winterhold.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''Those interested in learning more about magic may consider joining the College of Winterhold.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenWinterholdShield.nif||[[File:SR-load-Those interested in learning more about magic.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====[[Skyrim:Companions|Companions]]====
|-
|''Among the Companions' most treasured artifacts are the fragments of [[Skyrim:Wuuthrad|Wuuthrad]], the axe that [[Lore:Ysgramor|Ysgramor]] himself wielded when leading [[Lore:Five_Hundred_Companions|the Five Hundred]].''||rowspan=3|Weapons\AxeofYsgramor\{{zwsp}}1stPersonAxeofYsgramor.nif||[[File:SR-load-Among the Companions' most treasured artifacts.jpg|96px]]||rowspan=4| In [[Skyrim:Whiterun|Whiterun]], 9% chance.
|-
|''Nobody knows who built the [[Skyrim:Skyforge|Skyforge]], where the Companions' weapons are made. Its discovery led to the building of Jorrvaskr and the Companions as we know them today.''||[[File:SR-load-Nobody knows who built the Skyforge.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''The Circle is a small group of the most trusted and accomplished warriors from among the ranks of the Companions.''||[[File:SR-load-The Circle is a small group.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''The Companions trace their legacy back to the original Five Hundred Companions of Ysgramor, who led the first humans to Skyrim and eventually settled all of Tamriel.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenStatueYsgramor.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Companions trace their legacy.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''[[Skyrim:Kodlak_Whitemane|Kodlak Whitemane]] is the Harbinger of the Companions. He does not give orders, but his word is highly respected both inside Jorrvaskr and through all the nine Holds.''||Armor\Wolf\{{zwsp}}Hat_GO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Kodlak Whitemane is the Harbinger of the Companions.jpg|96px]]||In Whiterun, have not yet found all the [[Skyrim:Fragment of Wuuthrad|fragments of Wuuthrad]] in [[Skyrim:Purity of Revenge|Purity of Revenge]], 9% chance.
|-
|''Tamriel's [[Lore:Fighters_Guild|Fighters Guild]] has no presence in Skyrim. Instead, warriors seeking adventure and kinship may join the Companions, in Whiterun.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenWhiterunShield.nif||[[File:SR-load-Tamriel's Fighters Guild has no presence in Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====[[Skyrim:Dark Brotherhood|Dark Brotherhood]]====
|-
|''A Dark Brotherhood assassin practices the art of murder, and must be willing to pay for that crime... with gold, a jail sentence, or even more bloodshed.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleDarkElf.nif||[[File:SR-load-A Dark Brotherhood assassin practices.jpg|96px]]||In or near Falkreath Sanctuary or in Dawnstar Sanctuary, 51% chance.
|-
|''[[Skyrim:Astrid|Astrid]] is the leader of the Dark Brotherhood Sanctuary, and her word is law.''||Weapons\BladeofWoe\{{zwsp}}1stPersonBladeofWoe.nif||[[File:SR-load-Astrid is the leader.jpg|96px]]||In or near Falkreath Sanctuary, Astrid is not yet dead, 51% chance.
|-
|''It is said that rumors of the Dark Brotherhood's demise may have been premature, as members of the shadowy organization have been sighted near Dawnstar...''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleDarkElf.nif||[[File:SR-load-It is said that rumors.jpg|96px]]||In Dawnstar Sanctuary, [[Skyrim:Hail Sithis!|Hail Sithis!]] completed, 51% chance.
|-
|''It is said that the only way to join the Dark Brotherhood is to be contacted directly, and the shadowy group of assassins is very selective in its recruiting...''||Clutter\DBhood\{{zwsp}}DBDoor01.nif||[[File:SR-load-It is said that the only way to join the Dark Brotherhood.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Mortals often represent [[Lore:Sithis|Sithis]] as a skeletal being, to signify His relationship to death. In truth, the Dread Lord is formless, and infinite as [[Lore:Void|the Void]].''||Clutter\DBhood\{{zwsp}}DBStainglass01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Mortals often represent Sithis.jpg|96px]]||In or near Falkreath Sanctuary or in Dawnstar Sanctuary, Astrid is not yet dead, 51% chance.
|-
|''So long as there is a Listener to hear the [[Skyrim:Night_Mother|Night Mother's]] voice, the Dark Brotherhood will endure...''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenNMCoffin01.nif||[[File:SR-load-So long as there is a Listener.jpg|96px]]||In [[Skyrim:Dawnstar Sanctuary|Dawnstar Sanctuary]], 51% chance.
|-
|''"Sweet Mother, sweet Mother, send your child unto me, for the sins of the unworthy must be baptized in blood and fear." -- chant from the Dark Brotherhood's [[Lore:Black_Sacrament|Black Sacrament]] ||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSinister01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Sweet Mother, sweet Mother.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''The Dark Brotherhood was once bound by a set of rules called [[Lore:The_Five_Tenets|the Five Tenets]], but they have long since been abandoned.''||Clutter\DBhood\{{zwsp}}DBTenets01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Dark Brotherhood was once bound.jpg|96px]]||In or near [[Skyrim:Dark Brotherhood Sanctuary|Falkreath Sanctuary]], 51% chance.
|-
|''The Dark Brotherhood [[Skyrim:Dawnstar Sanctuary|Sanctuary in Dawnstar]] is now an ancient ruin, its ominous Black Door feared and avoided by the city's residents.''||Clutter\DBhood\{{zwsp}}DBDoor01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Dark Brotherhood Sanctuary in Dawnstar.jpg|96px]]||In [[Skyrim:Dawnstar Sanctuary|Dawnstar Sanctuary]], 51% chance.
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Dark Brotherhood Sanctuary|Sanctuary in Skyrim's Pine Forest]] is the Dark Brotherhood's last remaining refuge in all of Tamriel.''||Clutter\DBhood\{{zwsp}}DBDoor01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Sanctuary in Skyrim's Pine Forest.jpg|96px]]||In or near [[Skyrim:Dark Brotherhood Sanctuary|Falkreath Sanctuary]], 51% chance.
|-
|''The Dark Brotherhood was once greatly feared and respected, but the organization is now but a shadow of its former self.''||Clutter\DBhood\{{zwsp}}DBDoor01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Dark Brotherhood was once greatly feared.jpg|96px]]||In or near Falkreath Sanctuary or in Dawnstar Sanctuary, Astrid is not yet dead, 51% chance.
|-
|rowspan=2|''Those wishing to contact the Dark Brotherhood for an assassination must perform the Black Sacrament, an ancient and taboo ritual.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenNMCoffin01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Those wishing to contact the Dark Brotherhood (open).jpg|96px]]||rowspan=2| In or near Falkreath Sanctuary or in Dawnstar Sanctuary, [[Skyrim:Whispers in the Dark|Whispers in the Dark]] completed, 51% chance.
|-
||Clutter\NightMother\{{zwsp}}NMCoffin01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Those wishing to contact the Dark Brotherhood (closed).jpg|96px]]
