!colspan=4|
====By Era====
|-
|''In {{Year|3E 389}} Emperor [[Lore:Uriel Septim VII|Uriel VII]] was imprisoned by his Imperial Battlemage, [[Lore:Jagar Tharn|Jagar Tharn]], who then [[Lore:Imperial Simulacrum|impersonated him for years]].''||Weapons\MQDragonPriest\{{zwsp}}MQ_DragonPriestStaff.nif||[[File:SR-load-In 3E 389 Emperor Uriel VII.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Pelagius III, also known as Pelagius the Mad, was Jarl of Solitude before ascending to the throne of the Emperor in {{Year|3E 145}}.''||Armor\Steel\{{zwsp}}HelmetSteelGO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Pelagius III, also known as Pelagius the Mad.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Tiber Septim|Tiber Septim]] brought peace to [[Lore:Tamriel|Tamriel]] in {{Year|2E 896}}, by conquering all of the known world. Thus began the [[Lore:Third_Era|Third Era]].''||Armor\Orcish\{{zwsp}}OrcishShield.nif||[[File:SR-load-Tiber Septim brought peace.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{CC|The Cause|par=1}}''The [[Lore:Ayleids|Ayleids]] were a race of powerful Elves, whose culture was rich with magic and mystery. They were the first to establish an empire in Tamriel, but have not been seen since the First Era. Their ancient ruins dot the landscape of Cyrodiil.''||CreationClub\BGSSSE067\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenAyleids.nif||{{huh}}||Will not appear (see [[#Bugs|Bugs]]).
|-
|''The Fourth Era began 200 years ago when [[Lore:Martin_Septim|Martin Septim]] sacrificed himself to save the world from the [[Lore:Oblivion_Crisis|Oblivion Crisis]].''||Weapons\Iron\{{zwsp}}1stPersonWarHammer.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Fourth Era began 200 years ago.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{CC|The Cause|par=1}}''The Oblivion Crisis was a war with the Daedra at the end of the Third Era. Aided by the Mythic Dawn, the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon opened many Oblivion Gates throughout Tamriel, and nearly caused its destruction. The war was ultimately won by Martin Septim and the Hero of Kvatch.''||CreationClub\BGSSSE067\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenOblivionGate.nif||{{huh}}||Will not appear (see [[#Bugs|Bugs]]).
|-
|''The [[Lore:War of the Red Diamond|War of the Red Diamond]] began in {{Year|3E 121}} when [[Lore:Uriel Septim III|Uriel III]] captured the throne with his mother, Queen Potema. It ended in {{Year|3E 127}} with their defeat at the [[Lore:Siege of Solitude|Siege of Solitude]].''||Armor\Iron\{{zwsp}}ShieldHeavy.nif||[[File:SR-load-The War of the Red Diamond.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|

====[[Lore:Skyrim|Skyrim]]'s History====
|-
|''Legend holds that the highest ranking Dragon Priests were granted [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest Mask|magical masks]] - strange artifacts that defy the laws of time, and grant their wearers powerful enchantments.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaskAltar01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Legend holds that the highest ranking Dragon Priests.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''"Maw unleashing razor snow, Of dragons from the blue brought down, Births the walking winter's woe, The High King in his [[Skyrim:Jagged Crown|Jagged Crown]]." -- Ancient Nord Verse||Armor\BoneCrown\{{zwsp}}BoneCrownGO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Maw unleashing razor snow.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Nord belief holds that the honored dead live forever in [[Lore:Sovngarde|Sovngarde]].''||Architecture\Sovengarde\{{zwsp}}SovngardeStatue01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Nord belief holds.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Skyrim legend tells of a hero known as the Dragonborn, a warrior with the body of a mortal and soul of a dragon, whose destiny it is to destroy the evil dragon Alduin.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenAlduinWall.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skyrim legend tells of a hero.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The [[Skyrim:Greybeards|Greybeards]] of [[Lore:High_Hrothgar|High Hrothgar]] follow the teachings of [[Lore:Jurgen_Windcaller|Jurgen Windcaller]], who believed the power of the Voice was [[Lore:Way of the Voice|a means of attaining enlightenment]].''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenWCTomb01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Greybeards of High Hrothgar.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The most famous hero of Skyrim is Tiber Septim, who conquered all of Tamriel and founded the [[Lore:Septim_Dynasty|Septim dynasty]] of emperors.''||Weapons\Iron\{{zwsp}}1stPersonIronClaymore.nif||[[File:SR-load-The most famous hero of Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====Skyrim's Geography====
|-
|''Each of the nine Holds is governed by a Jarl. The Jarls are largely independent, but they swear fealty to Skyrim's High King.''||Armor\BoneCrown\{{zwsp}}BoneCrownGO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Each of the nine Holds.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Skyrim is home to the Nords, a fierce, hardy people that value honor and prowess in battle.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenStatueYsgramor.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skyrim is home to the Nords.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The highest mountain in all of Tamriel is Skyrim's [[Skyrim:Throat_of_the_World|Throat of the World]]. The reclusive Greybeards live near the top, in the ancient monastery of High Hrothgar.''||Actors\Male\{{zwsp}}GreyBeardStatic.nif||[[File:SR-load-The highest mountain in all of Tamriel.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''There are nine Holds in Skyrim: Eastmarch, Falkreath, Haafingar, Hjaalmarch, the Pale, the Reach, the Rift, Whiterun, and Winterhold.''||Clutter\CivilWar\{{zwsp}}CivilWarMap01.nif||[[File:SR-load-There are nine Holds in Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''When the High King dies, the Jarls of Skyrim convene a [[Lore:Moot|Moot]] to elect a new High King.''||Architecture\WhiteRun\WRClutter\{{zwsp}}WRThrone01Static.nif||[[File:SR-load-When the High King dies.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====[[Skyrim:Solstheim|{{Anchor|Solstheim}}]]{{DB|par=1}}====
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Skaal Village|Skaal Village]], near the eastern coast of Solstheim, is home to an ancient offshoot tribe of Nords known as the [[Lore:Skaal|Skaal]].''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSkaal01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skaal Village, near the eastern coast.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''Solstheim was part of Skyrim until the High King gave it to Morrowind in {{Year|4E 16}} to serve as a refuge for the Dunmer after the events of the [[Lore:Red_Year|Red Year]].''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenAdventure02.nif||[[File:SR-load-Solstheim was part of Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||Player is in Solstheim and has completed stage 100 of the Dragonborn initialization quest''or'' 4% chance of appearing under any conditions.{{VN|Conditions may be buggy—needs in-game verification.}}
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''Strange flora native to Morrowind have sprouted up in the ash that blankets the southern reaches of Solstheim.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenLocalGoods01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Strange flora native to Morrowind.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''The ancient Nords of Solstheim sealed their tombs with Stalhrim, a form of enchanted ice as hard as stone. The Skaal are the only ones who know the secret of crafting armor and weapons out of Stalhrim.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenStahlrim01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The ancient Nords of Solstheim.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''The ashfall from Red Mountain has driven much of Solstheim's native wildlife into the northern half of the island.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBurntWoods01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The ashfall from Red Mountain.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Thirsk_Mead_Hall|Thirsk Mead Hall]] was founded by [[Lore:Hrothmund the Red|Hrothmund]], who originally left the Skaal in order to live the lifestyle of ancient Nord warriors in the wilderness.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenThirsk01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Thirsk Mead Hall was founded by Hrothmund.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''The island of Solstheim is located to the north-east of Skyrim. The "[[Skyrim:Northern Maiden|Northern Maiden]]" out of Windhelm is known to occasionally take passengers back and forth.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenAdventure02.nif||[[File:SR-load-The island of Solstheim.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Tamriel.
|-
!colspan=4|
====The Present ({{Year|4E 201}})====
|-
|''Agents of the high elven [[Lore:Aldmeri Dominion|Aldmeri Dominion]] are known as [[Skyrim:Thalmor|Thalmor]]. They maintain an [[Skyrim:Thalmor Embassy|embassy]] in Skyrim, and have been known to secretly capture and imprison any Nords who question their doctrines or beliefs.''||Clothes\Thalmor\{{zwsp}}ThalmorBootsGO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Agents of the high elven Aldmeri Dominion.jpg|96px]]||
|- resen
|''Many of Skyrim's Nords harbor a bittertment of all elvenkind, who they've battled with throughout history. The [[Lore:Great War|Great War]] may be over, but its horrors are still fresh in the minds of the conflict's survivors...''||Weapons\Elven\{{zwsp}}1stPersonElvenBattleAxe.nif||[[File:SR-load-Many of Skyrim's Nords harbor a bitter resentment.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Only by signing the peace treaty known as the [[Lore:White-Gold Concordat|White-Gold Concordat]] was the Empire able to survive the onslaught of the high elven Aldmeri Dominion, and thus end the Great War.''||Weapons\Elven\{{zwsp}}1stPersonElvenMace.nif||[[File:SR-load-Only by signing the peace treaty.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Skyrim is engaged in a [[Lore:Stormcloak Rebellion|bloody civil conflict]] between the rebel Stormcloaks and soldiers of the Imperial Legion.''||Armor\NordPlate\{{zwsp}}Cuirass_GO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skyrim is engaged in a bloody civil conflict.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Skyrim is in turmoil because the Stormcloaks believe their Nord way of life is at risk, while the Imperials believe Skyrim is a part of the Empire, and must follow its laws and customs.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenWindhelmShield.nif||[[File:SR-load-Skyrim is in turmoil.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The High King of Skyrim, [[Skyrim:High King Torygg|Torygg]], was recently killed by Ulfric Stormcloak, who used the ancient power of the [[Skyrim:Thu'um|Thu'um]] to nearly shout Torygg to pieces.''||Actors\Male\{{zwsp}}GreyBeardStatic.nif||[[File:SR-load-The High King of Skyrim.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====[[Lore:Races|Races]]====
|-
|''[[Lore:Argonian|Argonians]] are the reptilian natives of the province of [[Lore:Black Marsh|Black Marsh]].''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenArgonian.nif||[[File:SR-load-Argonians are the reptilian natives.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''At the center of the [[Lore:Dunmer|Dunmer]] province of Morrowind lies the Red Mountain, the largest volcano in all of Tamriel.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleDarkElf.nif||[[File:SR-load-At the center of the Dunmer province.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Skyrim:Bonemold|Bonemold]] armor is a type of Dunmer armor crafted out of bone and resins.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBonemold01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Bonemold armor is a type of Dunmer armor.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|''[[Lore:Breton|Bretons]] are natives of [[Lore:High Rock|High Rock]]. It is home to the oldest known structure in all of Tamriel, the [[Lore:Adamantine Tower|Adamantine Tower]], also known as Direnni Tower.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenBretonMage.nif||[[File:SR-load-Bretons are natives of High Rock.jpg|96px]]||
|- 
|''Dark elves, also known as Dunmer, are natives of [[Lore:Morrowind|Morrowind]] - a land many consider alien and inhospitable.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleDarkElf.nif||[[File:SR-load-Dark elves, also known as Dunmer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Altmer|High elves]], also known as Altmer, are natives of [[Lore:Summerset Isle|Summerset Isle]]. It is an ancient land shrouded in mystery. ||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleHighElf.nif||[[File:SR-load-High elves, also known as Altmer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Imperial|Imperials]] are natives of [[Lore:Cyrodiil|Cyrodiil]], the cosmopolitan heartland of the [[Lore:Empire|Empire]].''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenFemaleImperial.nif||[[File:SR-load-Imperials are natives of Cyrodiil.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Khajiit|Khajiit]] are a feline race native to [[Lore:Elsweyr|Elsweyr]]. It is infamous for producing [[Skyrim:Moon Sugar|Moon Sugar]], which can be refined into [[Skyrim:Skooma|Skooma]].''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenKhajiitThief.nif||[[File:SR-load-Khajiit are a feline race.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Orc|Orcs]], also known as Orsimer, are natives of [[Lore:Orsinium|Orsinium]], a small mountain kingdom between Hammerfell and Skyrim. It has been sacked and rebuilt many times.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleOrc_1.nif||[[File:SR-load-Orcs, also known as Orsimer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Redguard|Redguards]] are natives of [[Lore:Hammerfell|Hammerfell]]. Its cities hug the edges of the great Alik'r Desert.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMaleRedguard_1.nif||[[File:SR-load-Redguards are natives of Hammerfell.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''Some tales tell of ancient [[Lore:Nord|Nord]] heroes whose Voices were powerful enough to tame and ride [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragons]].''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDragonRiding01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Some tales tell of ancient Nord heroes.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player has completed The Temple of Miraak.
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''The Dunmer of Morrowind construct [[Skyrim:Chitin|chitin]] armor out of the shells of native insects layered with resinous glues.''||DLC02\LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenChitin01.nif||[[File:SR-load-The Dunmer of Morrowind construct chitin.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing if the player is in Solstheim.
|-
|''[[Lore:Bosmer|Wood Elves]], also known as Bosmer, are natives of [[Lore:Valenwood|Valenwood]]. This jungle nation is home to giant, migratory trees that house their cities.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenFemaleWoodElf.nif||[[File:SR-load-Wood Elves, also known as Bosmer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====[[Lore:Daedric Princes|Daedric Princes]]====
|-
|{{DB|par=1}}''[[Lore:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]] is the realm of [[Skyrim:Hermaeus Mora|Hermaeus Mora]], the Daedric Prince of Fate and Knowledge. Many who come here seeking forbidden knowledge remain forever.''||DLC02\Dungeons\Apocrypha\Clutter\{{zwsp}}ApoHMShrine01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Apocrypha is the realm of Hermaeus Mora.jpg|96px]]||6% chance of appearing and the player is in Solstheim or Apocrypha and Hermaeus Mora intro scene has played.{{huh|1=GetVMQuestVariable(DLC2BookDungeonController, ::bHMIntroScenePlayed_var) == 1}}
|-
|''[[Lore:Azura|Azura]] is the daedric prince of dusk and dawn, and one of the few not considered to be inherently evil.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}ShrineOfAzura01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Azura is the daedric prince of dusk and dawn.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Boethiah|Boethiah]] is the daedric prince of deceit, conspiracy, and secret plots of murder. Many dark elves consider him to be their god-ancestor.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDSBoethiah01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Boethiah is the daedric prince of deceit.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Clavicus Vile|Clavicus Vile]] is the daedric prince of power. He is fond of enticing mortals with tempting pacts... which they later come to regret.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenClavicusVileMask.nif||[[File:SR-load-Clavicus Vile is the daedric prince of power.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Daedric princes are god-like beings that inhabit the plane of [[Lore:Oblivion|Oblivion]]. Most are considered evil, forcing their worshippers to build their shrines far from civilized places.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}MalacathStatue01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Daedric princes are god-like beings.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Hermaeus Mora|Hermaeus Mora]] is the daedric prince of fate, knowledge and memory. In his rare dealings with mortals, he often chooses to appear as a grotesque mass of tentacles.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenRunedStand01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Hermaeus Mora is the daedric prince of fate.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Malacath|Malacath]] is the daedric prince of curses and the spurned. Many orcs worship him as their god-king. ||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}MalacathStatue01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Malacath is the daedric prince of curses.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Mehrunes Dagon|Mehrunes Dagon]] is the daedric prince of destruction, revolution and ambition. He caused the [[Lore:Oblivion Crisis|Oblivion Crisis]] when he attempted to enter Tamriel in his true, and terrible, form.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenMRaltar01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Mehrunes Dagon is the daedric prince of destruction.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Mephala|Mephala]] is the daedric prince of lies, secrets and plots... and thoroughly enjoys meddling in the affairs of mortals.''||Weapons\EbonyBlade\{{zwsp}}1stPersonEbonyBlade.nif||[[File:SR-load-Mephala is the daedric prince of lies.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Meridia|Meridia]] despises undead in any form, and is one of the few daedric princes not considered to be wholly evil.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}StatueofMeridia01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Meridia despises undead in any form.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Namira|Namira]] is the daedric prince of darkness and revulsion, and is frequently associated with disease, spiders, insects, slugs and other repulsive creatures.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}StatueNamira.nif||[[File:SR-load-Namira is the daedric prince of darkness and revulsion.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Nocturnal|Nocturnal]] is the daedric mistress of stealth and shadow, and a patron to thieves.''||Clothes\Nocturnal\{{zwsp}}Statue.nif||[[File:SR-load-Nocturnal is the daedric mistress of stealth and shadow.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Peryite|Peryite]] is the daedric prince of tasks, order and pestilence. He is considered one of the weakest of the princes, despite being depicted as a dragon.''||Armor\Spellbreaker\{{zwsp}}Spellbreaker.nif||[[File:SR-load-Peryite is the daedric prince of tasks.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Sanguine|Sanguine]] is the daedric prince of hedonism, debauchery and dark indulgences. He is more likely than most princes to take an interest in mortal affairs.''||Weapons\SanguineRose\{{zwsp}}SanguineRose.nif||[[File:SR-load-Sanguine is the daedric prince of hedonism.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Sheogorath|Sheogorath]] is the daedric prince of madness. He is utterly unpredictable, and may hinder or help any mortal unlucky enough to cross his path.''||Weapons\Wabbajack\{{zwsp}}Wabbajack.nif||[[File:SR-load-Sheogorath is the daedric prince of madness.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The daedric prince [[Lore:Hircine|Hircine]] is also known as the Huntsman of the Princes, and the Father of Manbeasts. He can call upon the Wild Hunt to punish those who defy him.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}ShrineofHircine.nif||[[File:SR-load-The daedric prince Hircine.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Vaermina|Vaermina]] is the daedric prince of dreams, nightmares and evil omens.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}StatueVaermina.nif||[[File:SR-load-Vaermina is the daedric prince of dreams.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====The [[Lore:Aedra|Divines]]====
|-
|''[[Lore:Akatosh|Akatosh]] is the god of time and the chief deity of the Nine Divines. He is depicted as a dragon, and chose that form to battle Mehrunes Dagon in the Oblivion Crisis.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenShrineAkatosh.nif||[[File:SR-load-Akatosh is the god of time.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Arkay|Arkay]] is the god of burials and funeral rites. His priests root out undead and necromancy wherever it may be found. Every Skyrim city has a Hall of the Dead dedicated to him.''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineArkay.nif||[[File:SR-load-Arkay is the god of burials and funeral rites.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Dibella|Dibella]] is the goddess of beauty. She has a [[Skyrim:Temple of Dibella|temple in Markarth]] that is devoted to women.''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineDibella.nif||[[File:SR-load-Dibella is the goddess of beauty.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Julianos|Julianos]] is the god of wisdom and logic. Usually associated with magic, he is often revered by wizards. He has a shrine in the [[Skyrim:Temple of the Divines|Temple of the Divines]] in Solitude.''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineJulianos.nif||[[File:SR-load-Julianos is the god of wisdom and logic.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Kynareth|Kynareth]] is the goddess of the air, wind and sky. She has a [[Skyrim:Temple of Kynareth|temple in Whiterun]].''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineKynareth.nif||[[File:SR-load-Kynareth is the goddess of the air.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|rowspan=2|''[[Lore:Mara|Mara]] is the goddess of love and compassion. She has a [[Skyrim:Temple of Mara|temple in Riften]].''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineMara.nif||[[File:SR-load-Mara is the goddess of love and compassion (shrine).jpg|96px]]||
|-
||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}StatueMara01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Mara is the goddess of love and compassion (statue).jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Stendarr|Stendarr]] is the god of righteous rule by might and merciful forbearance. He has a shrine in the Temple of the Divines in Solitude.''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineStendarr.nif||[[File:SR-load-Stendarr is the god of righteous rule.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Talos|Talos]] is the hero-god of mankind. His worship is currently banned by the Empire, but that hasn't stopped the Nords of Skyrim from revering him.''||Clutter\Statues\{{zwsp}}StatueTalos01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Talos is the hero-god of mankind.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''[[Lore:Zenithar|Zenithar]] is the god of work and commerce. He has a shrine in the Temple of the Divines in Solitude.''||Clutter\Shrines\{{zwsp}}ShrineZenithar.nif||[[File:SR-load-Zenithar is the god of work and commerce.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====The [[Lore:Blades|Blades]]====
|-
|''Although they later became the dedicated protectors of the Emperor of Tamriel, the Blades began their existence as renowned dragonslayers.''||rowspan=2| Armor\Blades\{{zwsp}}HelmetBladesGO.nif||[[File:SR-load-Although they later became the dedicated protectors.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''The Blades have long since disbanded, and the organization's few remaining members have gone into hiding. The Emperor is now protected by a special security force - the [[Skyrim:Penitus_Oculatus|Penitus Oculatus]].''||[[File:SR-load-The Blades have long since disbanded.jpg|96px]]||
|-
!colspan=4|
====The [[Lore:Dwemer|Dwemer]]====
|-
|''"But our brethren, the Dwemer, scorned the Daedra, and mocked our foolish rituals, and preferred instead their gods of Reason and Logic." -- [[Lore:Vivec|Vivec]]||Dungeons\Dwemer\Clutter\{{zwsp}}DweCenturionBust01.nif||[[File:SR-load-But our brethren, the Dwemer.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Dwarven ruins are dangerous to explore because of devious traps and hazardous machinery, to say nothing of the denizens that may dwell within...''||Dungeons\Dwemer\Clutter\{{zwsp}}DweCenturionBust01.nif||[[File:SR-load-Dwarven ruins are dangerous to explore.jpg|96px]]||
|-
|''Many Steam Animunculi remain active, making the exploration of dwarven ruins a dangerous prospect.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSteam.nif||[[File:SR-load-Many Steam Animunculi remain active.jpg|96px]]||rowspan=3| In [[Skyrim:Avanchnzel|Avanchnzel]], [[Skyrim:Alftand|Alftand]], the [[Skyrim:Ruins of Bthalft|Ruins of Bthalft]], [[Skyrim:Bthardamz|Bthardamz]], [[Skyrim:Irkngthand|Irkngthand]], [[Skyrim:Kagrenzel|Kagrenzel]], [[Skyrim:Nchuand-Zel|Nchuand-Zel]], or [[Skyrim:Raldbthar|Raldbthar]], 16% chance.
|-
|''The dwarves of Tamriel disappeared millennia ago and are presumed extinct.''||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenSphere.nif||[[File:SR-load-The dwarves of Tamriel.jpg|96px]]
|-
|''The dwarves were actually a race of [[Lore:Mer|elves]] known as the Dwemer, which roughly translates to "deep elves."||LoadScreenArt\{{zwsp}}LoadScreenDwarvenSpider.nif||[[File:SR-load-The dwarves were actually a race of elves.jpg|96px]]
